Now:
- b=1: y=K. Then expression = a + x/K. Since 1≤x=201/a≤201<K, the fractional part x/K is nonzero, so not integer.
- b=K: y=1. Then expression = a/K + x. Since 1≤a≤201<K, not integer.
- b=101: y=101. Then expression = (a+x)/101. We need 101 | a+x, where x=201/a. Test a values:
a=1 -> x=201 -> sum=202=2·101;
a=3 -> x=67 -> sum=70;
a=67 -> x=3 -> sum=70;
a=201 -> x=1 -> sum=202=2·101.
Thus two pairs: (1,101), (201,101).
